NAME
       semget, semop, semctl - semaphores

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/sem.h>

       int semget(key_t key, int nsems, int flag);
       int semop(int id, struct sembuf *ops, size_t nops);
       int semctl(int id, int num, int cmd, ...);

DESCRIPTION
       System V semaphores, used to coordinate processes that share
       memory. semop applies a list of operations atomically: either
       all of them happen or the caller waits.

RETURN VALUE
       0 or an id on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       EAGAIN   IPC_NOWAIT was set and the operation would block
       EINVAL   bad id or index
       EINTR    a signal arrived while waiting

SEE ALSO
       shmget(2), futex(2), semtest(1)
